14-/** `clerkLimit` has two decimals ("1.50"), or is "" when there is no limit; `floor` has two decimals;
15- *  `terms` is a whole number of days ("14"), and `gradeTerms` the terms in force for each grade (its own, else the sheet's); `latePct` is a percent with two decimals ("0.00");
16: *  `policyDate` is yyyy-mm-dd, or "" when there is none (the sheet's today is the policy date); `periodNumberingFrom` is yyyy-mm-dd, or "" when numbering by period is off; `cap` has two decimals, or is "" when there is none; `graceDays` is a whole number of days (not dated), or "" when closing periods by today is off; `entryDate` is yyyy-mm-dd, or "" when it is off (a new claim left undated takes the sheet's today); `pot` has two decimals (not dated), or is "" when there is none; `alertThreshold` has two decimals (not dated), or is "" when alerts are off; `escalateAfter` is a whole number of days (not dated), or "" when escalation is off; `reviewSla` is a whole number of days (not dated), or "" when there is none; `pendingSla` is a whole number of days (not dated), or "" when there is none; `maxOpen` is the most OPEN or PENDING claims a person may have (not dated), or "" when there is none; `proofKinds` are the proof kinds, comma separated (not dated), or "" when there are none; `parent` is the id of the sheet whose rates are used where this one has none (not dated), or "" when there is none; `fiscalStartMonth` is the month (1 to 12) the sheet's fiscal year starts on (not dated; "1" unless set).
